  "modeRationale": "These are the modes Debian and Ubuntu base-files give the same five directories. A mount point's own mode is invisible once something is mounted over it, so matching the base system is the only reason to prefer one number over another. /tmp is the exception that matters: nothing is mounted over it here, so its 1777 is the mode processes will actually see.",
