  "status": "RUNTIME-MOUNT-POINT-DIRECTORIES-AUDITED-AND-REQUIRED-NO-IMAGE-PRODUCED",
  "whatWouldBeNeeded": "One successor production of the two arm64 replicas, run exactly once, and a boot attempt only if the two images are byte-identical and carry all five directories.",
  "whyThisRecordExists": "The one MAC.3 closed-local boot reached PID 1 and froze, because the image carries no directory for systemd to mount /proc, /sys and /dev on. The console named three. This record names the five the guest's own systemd actually needs, so the successor image is not built against a list that came out of one transcript."
